From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:35:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] librustutils: system_properties under atl_android_userspace

ATL builds device Rust for the host triple (target_os = linux) and
provides bionic system properties in its C library, so the module the
ATL Android-userspace build needs is enabled by its --cfg.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ATL-specific cfg]
Patch-Reason: target_os is the host OS on ATL; only the source gate can tell this build apart, the converter passes the cfg
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 lib.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib.rs b/lib.rs
index a1beab553174229f073edc243178826f35fb1af2..647604f2d9733987fe94c250abf364df3bceee53 100644
--- a/lib.rs
+++ b/lib.rs
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #[cfg(target_os = "android")]
 pub mod sockets;
 
-#[cfg(target_os = "android")]
+#[cfg(any(target_os = "android", atl_android_userspace))]
 pub mod system_properties;
 
 #[cfg(target_os = "android")]
